\s1 The Invasion of Locusts
\p \v 1 \rb This is the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joel|יוֹאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Pethuel|פְּתוּאֵֽל׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 2 \rb Hear|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb this|זֹאת֙\rb*, \rb O elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֔ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb and give ear|וְהַֽאֲזִ֔ינוּ\rb*, \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who dwell|יוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Has anything like this|זֹּאת֙\rb* \rb ever happened|הֶהָ֤יְתָה\rb* \rb in your days|בִּֽימֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb or|וְאִ֖ם\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֹֽתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 3 \rb Tell|סַפֵּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb to your children|לִבְנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb let your children|וּבְנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb tell it to their children|לִבְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their children|וּבְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to the next|אַחֵֽר׃\rb* \rb generation|לְד֥וֹר\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb What the devouring locust|הַגָּזָם֙\rb* \rb has left|יֶ֤תֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb the swarming locust|הָֽאַרְבֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb has eaten|אָכַ֣ל\rb*;
\q1 \rb what the swarming locust|הָאַרְבֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb has left|וְיֶ֥תֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb the young locust|הַיָּ֑לֶק\rb* \rb has eaten|אָכַ֣ל\rb*;
\q1 \rb and what the young locust|הַיֶּ֔לֶק\rb* \rb has left|וְיֶ֣תֶר\rb*,
\q2 \rb the destroying locust|הֶחָסִֽיל׃\rb* \rb has eaten|אָכַ֖ל\rb*.\f + \fr 1:4 \ft The precise identification of the four kinds of locusts mentioned here is uncertain.\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb Wake up|הָקִ֤יצוּ\rb*, \rb you drunkards|שִׁכּוֹרִים֙\rb*, \rb and weep|וּבְכ֔וּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb wail|וְהֵילִ֖לוּ\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb you drinkers|שֹׁ֣תֵי\rb* \rb of wine|יָ֑יִן\rb*,
\q1 \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the sweet wine|עָסִ֕יס\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it has been cut off|נִכְרַ֖ת\rb* \rb from your mouth|מִפִּיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb a nation|גוֹי֙\rb* \rb has invaded|עָלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb My land|אַרְצִ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb powerful|עָצ֖וּם\rb* \rb and without|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb number|מִסְפָּ֑ר\rb*;
\q1 \rb its teeth|שִׁנָּיו֙\rb* \rb are the teeth|שִׁנֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of a lion|אַרְיֵ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and its fangs are the fangs|וּֽמְתַלְּע֥וֹת\rb* \rb of a lioness|לָבִ֖יא\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb It has laid|שָׂ֤ם\rb* \rb waste|לְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb My grapevine|גַּפְנִי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and splintered|לִקְצָפָ֑ה\rb* \rb My fig tree|וּתְאֵנָתִ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \rb It has stripped off the bark|חָשֹׂ֤ף\rb*\rb |חֲשָׂפָהּ֙\rb* \rb and thrown it away|וְהִשְׁלִ֔יךְ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the branches|שָׂרִיגֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb have turned white|הִלְבִּ֖ינוּ\rb*.
\s1 A Call to Mourning
\q1 \v 8 \rb Wail|אֱלִ֕י\rb* \rb like a virgin|כִּבְתוּלָ֥ה\rb* \rb dressed|חֲגֻֽרַת־\rb* \rb in sackcloth|שַׂ֖ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb grieving for|עַל־\rb* \rb the husband|בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb of her youth|נְעוּרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb Grain and drink offerings|מִנְחָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וָנֶ֖סֶךְ\rb* \rb have been cut off|הָכְרַ֥ת\rb*
\q2 \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*;
\q1 \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb are in mourning|אָֽבְלוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb those who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֖י\rb* \rb before the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb The field|שָׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb is ruined|שֻׁדַּ֣ד\rb*;
\q2 \rb the land|אֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb mourns|אָבְלָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the grain|דָּגָ֔ן\rb* \rb is destroyed|שֻׁדַּ֣ד\rb*,
\q2 \rb the new wine|תִּיר֖וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֻמְלַ֥ל\rb* \rb is dried up|הוֹבִ֥ישׁ\rb*, \rb and the oil fails|יִצְהָֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Be dismayed|הֹבִ֣ישׁוּ\rb*, \rb O farmers|אִכָּרִ֗ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb wail|הֵילִ֙ילוּ֙\rb*, \rb O vinedressers|כֹּֽרְמִ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the wheat|חִטָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb barley|שְׂעֹרָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the harvest|קְצִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \rb has perished|אָבַ֖ד\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb The grapevine|הַגֶּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb is dried up|הוֹבִ֔ישָׁה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the fig tree|וְהַתְּאֵנָ֖ה\rb* \rb is withered|אֻמְלָ֑לָה\rb*;
\q1 \rb the pomegranate|רִמּ֞וֹן\rb*,\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb palm|תָּמָ֣ר\rb*, \rb and apple|וְתַפּ֗וּחַ\rb*—
\q2 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the orchard|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*— \rb are withered|יָבֵ֔שׁוּ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Surely|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the joy|שָׂשׂ֖וֹן\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb mankind|אָדָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb has dried up|הֹבִ֥ישׁ\rb*.
\s1 A Call to Repentance
\r (\ref Amos 5:4–15|AMO 5:4-15\ref*; \ref Zephaniah 2:1–3|ZEP 2:1-3\ref*; \ref Luke 13:1–5|LUK 13:1-5\ref*)
\q1 \v 13 \rb Put on sackcloth|חִגְר֨וּ\rb* \rb and lament|וְסִפְד֜וּ\rb*, \rb O priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb wail|הֵילִ֙ילוּ֙\rb*, \rb O ministers|מְשָׁרְתֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the altar|מִזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Come|בֹּ֚אוּ\rb*, \rb spend the night|לִ֣ינוּ\rb* \rb in sackcloth|בַשַּׂקִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb O ministers|מְשָׁרְתֵ֖י\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהָ֑י\rb*,
\q1 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the grain|מִנְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb and drink offerings|וָנָֽסֶךְ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb are withheld|נִמְנַ֛ע\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Consecrate|קַדְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb a fast|צוֹם֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb proclaim|קִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb a solemn assembly|עֲצָרָ֔ה\rb*!
\q1 \rb Gather|אִסְפ֣וּ\rb* \rb the elders|זְקֵנִ֗ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the residents|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb to the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and cry out|וְזַעֲק֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Alas|אֲהָ֖הּ\rb* \rb for the day|לַיּ֑וֹם\rb*!
\q2 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is near|קָרוֹב֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb and it will come|יָבֽוֹא׃\rb*
\q2 \rb as destruction|וּכְשֹׁ֖ד\rb* \rb from the Almighty|מִשַׁדַּ֥י\rb*.\f + \fr 1:15 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shaddai\f*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Has not|הֲל֛וֹא\rb* \rb the food|אֹ֣כֶל\rb* \rb been cut off|נִכְרָ֑ת\rb*
\q2 \rb before|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb our very eyes|עֵינֵ֖ינוּ\rb* —
\q1 \rb joy|שִׂמְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb and gladness|וָגִֽיל׃\rb*
\q2 \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*?
\q1 \v 17 \rb The seeds|פְרֻד֗וֹת\rb* \rb lie shriveled|עָבְשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb the clods|מֶגְרְפֹ֣תֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb the storehouses|אֹֽצָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb are in ruins|נָשַׁ֙מּוּ֙\rb*;
\q1 \rb the granaries|מַמְּגֻר֑וֹת\rb* \rb are broken down|נֶהֶרְס֖וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the grain|דָּגָֽן׃\rb* \rb has withered away|הֹבִ֖ישׁ\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb How|מַה־\rb* \rb the cattle|בְהֵמָ֗ה\rb* \rb groan|נֶּאֶנְחָ֣ה\rb*!
\q2 \rb The herds|עֶדְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb wander in confusion|נָבֹ֙כוּ֙\rb*
\q1 \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they have no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb pasture|מִרְעֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb*.
\q2 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb* \rb the flocks|עֶדְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of sheep|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb* \rb are suffering|נֶאְשָֽׁמוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb To You|אֵלֶ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb I call|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb has consumed|אָֽכְלָה֙\rb* \rb the open|מִדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb pastures|נְא֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and flames|וְלֶ֣הָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb have scorched|לִהֲטָ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb Even|גַּם־\rb* \rb the beasts|בַּהֲמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb pant|תַּעֲר֣וֹג\rb* \rb for You|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the streams|אֲפִ֣יקֵי\rb* \rb of water|מָ֔יִם\rb* \rb have dried up|יָֽבְשׁוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and fire|וְאֵ֕שׁ\rb* \rb has consumed|אָכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb the open|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃פ\rb* \rb pastures|נְא֥וֹת\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 The Army of Locusts
\r (\ref Amos 7:1–9|AMO 7:1-9\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Blow|תִּקְע֨וּ\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָ֜ר\rb* \rb in Zion|בְּצִיּ֗וֹן\rb*;
\q2 \rb sound the alarm|וְהָרִ֙יעוּ֙\rb* \rb on My holy|קָדְשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb mountain|בְּהַ֣ר\rb*!
\q1 \rb Let all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb in the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb tremble|יִרְגְּז֕וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is coming|בָ֥א\rb*;
\q2 \rb indeed|כִּ֥י\rb*, \rb it is near|קָרֽוֹב׃\rb*—
\q1 \v 2 \rb a day|י֧וֹם\rb* \rb of darkness|חֹ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and gloom|וַאֲפֵלָ֗ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb a day|י֤וֹם\rb* \rb of clouds|עָנָן֙\rb* \rb and blackness|וַעֲרָפֶ֔ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb Like the dawn|כְּשַׁ֖חַר\rb* \rb overspreading|פָּרֻ֣שׂ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶֽהָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb a great|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb and strong|וְעָצ֔וּם\rb* \rb army appears|עַ֚ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb such as|כָּמֹ֗הוּ\rb* \rb never|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb was|נִֽהְיָה֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb old|הָ֣עוֹלָ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor will ever be|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb in ages to come|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |דּ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |וָדֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Before them|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb devours|אָ֣כְלָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and behind them|וְאַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb a flame|לֶֽהָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb scorches|תְּלַהֵ֣ט\rb*.
\q1 \rb The land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb before them|לְפָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb is like the Garden|כְּגַן־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֨דֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb but behind them|וְאַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb*, \rb it is like a desert|מִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb wasteland|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* —
\q2 \rb surely|וְגַם־\rb* \rb nothing|לֹא־\rb* \rb will|הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb escape|פְּלֵיטָ֖ה\rb* \rb them|לּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Their appearance|כְּמַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb is like that|מַרְאֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb of horses|סוּסִ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they gallop|יְרוּצֽוּן׃\rb* \rb like swift steeds|וּכְפָרָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb*.\f + \fr 2:4 \ft Or \fqa like charioteers \ft or \fqa like cavalry\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb With a sound like|כְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb that of chariots|מַרְכָּב֗וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb they bound|יְרַקֵּד֔וּן\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb*\rb |רָאשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb the mountaintops|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb like the crackling|כְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |לַ֣הַב\rb* \rb consuming|אֹכְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb stubble|קָ֑שׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb like a mighty|עָצ֔וּם\rb* \rb army|כְּעַ֣ם\rb* \rb deployed|עֱר֖וּךְ\rb* \rb for battle|מִלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Nations|עַמִּ֑ים\rb* \rb writhe in horror|יָחִ֣ילוּ\rb* \rb before them|מִפָּנָ֖יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb turns pale|קִבְּצ֥וּ\rb*\rb |פָארֽוּר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb They charge|יְרֻצ֔וּן\rb* \rb like mighty men|כְּגִבּוֹרִ֣ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb they scale|יַעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb the walls|חוֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb like men|כְּאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחָמָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Each one|וְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb marches|יֵֽלֵכ֔וּן\rb* \rb in formation|בִּדְרָכָיו֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb swerving|יְעַבְּט֖וּן\rb* \rb from the course|אֹרְחוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb They do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb jostle|יִדְחָק֔וּן\rb* \rb one|וְאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb another|אָחִיו֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb each|גֶּ֥בֶר\rb* \rb proceeds|יֵֽלֵכ֑וּן\rb*\rb |וּבְעַ֥ד\rb* \rb in his path|בִּמְסִלָּת֖וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They burst through|יִפֹּ֖לוּ\rb* \rb the defenses|הַשֶּׁ֛לַח\rb*,
\q2 \rb never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb breaking ranks|יִבְצָֽעוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb They storm|יָשֹׁ֗קּוּ\rb* \rb the city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb*;
\q2 \rb they run|יְרֻצ֔וּן\rb* \rb along the wall|בַּֽחוֹמָה֙\rb*;
\q1 \rb they climb|יַעֲל֑וּ\rb* \rb into houses|בַּבָּתִּ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb entering|יָבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb through|בְּעַ֧ד\rb* \rb windows|הַחַלּוֹנִ֛ים\rb* \rb like thieves|כַּגַּנָּֽב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Before them|לְפָנָיו֙\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb quakes|רָ֣גְזָה\rb*;
\q2 \rb the heavens|שָׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb tremble|רָעֲשׁ֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The sun|שֶׁ֤מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and moon|וְיָרֵ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb grow dark|קָדָ֔רוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the stars|וְכוֹכָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb lose|אָסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb their brightness|נָגְהָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The LORD|וַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb raises|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb His voice|קוֹלוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of His army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Indeed|כִּ֣י\rb*, \rb His camp|מַחֲנֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb is very|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb large|רַ֤ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb mighty are|עָצ֖וּם\rb* \rb those who obey|עֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb His command|דְבָר֑וֹ\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb is great|גָד֧וֹל\rb* \rb and very|מְאֹ֖ד\rb* \rb dreadful|וְנוֹרָ֥א\rb*.
\q2 \rb Who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can endure it|יְכִילֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*?
\s1 Return with All Your Heart
\q1 \v 12 “\rb Yet even|וְגַם־\rb* \rb now|עַתָּה֙\rb*,”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,
\q1 “\rb return|שֻׁ֥בוּ\rb* \rb to Me|עָדַ֖י\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבַבְכֶ֑ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb with fasting|וּבְצ֥וֹם\rb*, \rb weeping|וּבְבְכִ֖י\rb*, \rb and mourning|וּבְמִסְפֵּֽד׃\rb*.”
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb So rend|וְקִרְע֤וּ\rb* \rb your hearts|לְבַבְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb your garments|בִּגְדֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and return|וְשׁ֖וּבוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is gracious|חַנּ֤וּן\rb* \rb and compassionate|וְרַחוּם֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb slow|אֶ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb to anger|אַפַּ֙יִם֙\rb*, \rb abounding|וְרַב־\rb* \rb in loving devotion|חֶ֔סֶד\rb*.\f + \fr 2:13 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa chesed \ft are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as \fqa loving devotion\ft ; the range of meaning includes \fqa love\ft , \fqa goodness\ft , \fqa kindness\ft , \fqa faithfulness\ft , and \fqa mercy\ft , as well as \fqa loyalty to a covenant\ft .\f*
\q2 \rb And He relents|וְנִחָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb sending disaster|הָרָעָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb knows|יוֹדֵ֖עַ\rb*? \rb He may turn|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb and relent|וְנִחָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and leave|וְהִשְׁאִ֤יר\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָ֔ה\rb* \rb behind Him|אַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb* —
\q1 \rb grain|מִנְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb and drink offerings|וָנֶ֔סֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb Blow|תִּקְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Zion|בְּצִיּ֑וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb consecrate|קַדְּשׁוּ־\rb* \rb a fast|צ֖וֹם\rb*,
\q2 \rb proclaim|קִרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb a sacred assembly|עֲצָרָֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Gather|אִסְפוּ־\rb* \rb the people|עָ֞ם\rb*, \rb sanctify|קַדְּשׁ֤וּ\rb* \rb the congregation|קָהָל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb assemble|קִבְצ֣וּ\rb* \rb the aged|זְקֵנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb gather|אִסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb the children|עֽוֹלָלִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb even those nursing|וְיֹנְקֵ֖י\rb* \rb at the breast|שָׁדָ֑יִם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Let the bridegroom|חָתָן֙\rb* \rb leave|יֵצֵ֤א\rb* \rb his room|מֵֽחֶדְר֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the bride|וְכַלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb her chamber|מֵחֻפָּתָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Let the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֖י\rb* \rb before the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb weep|יִבְכּוּ֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb the portico|הָאוּלָם֙\rb* \rb and the altar|וְלַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*,
\q1 \rb saying|וְֽיֹאמְר֞וּ\rb*, “\rb Spare|ח֧וּסָה\rb* \rb Your people|עַמֶּ֗ךָ\rb*, \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb make|תִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb Your heritage|נַחֲלָתְךָ֤\rb* \rb a reproach|לְחֶרְפָּה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb an object of scorn|לִמְשָׁל־\rb* \rb among the nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb Why|לָ֚מָּה\rb* \rb should they say|יֹאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb among the peoples|בָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 ‘\rb Where|אַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*?’”
\s1 Restoration Promised
\q1 \v 18 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb became jealous|וַיְקַנֵּ֥א\rb* \rb for His land|לְאַרְצ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and He spared|וַיַּחְמֹ֖ל\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb His people|עַמּֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb His people|לְעַמּ֗וֹ\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I will send|שֹׁלֵ֤חַ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb grain|הַדָּגָן֙\rb*, \rb new wine|וְהַתִּיר֣וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb and oil|וְהַיִּצְהָ֔ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and by them|אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb you will be satisfied|וּשְׂבַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will never again|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb make you|אֶתֵּ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֥ם\rb*
\q2 \rb a reproach|חֶרְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb The northern army|הַצְּפוֹנִ֞י\rb* \rb I will drive away|אַרְחִ֣יק\rb* \rb from you|מֵעֲלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb banishing it|וְהִדַּחְתִּיו֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a barren|צִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and desolate|וּשְׁמָמָה֒\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*,
\q1 \rb its front|פָּנָ֗יו\rb* \rb ranks|אֶל־\rb* \rb into the Eastern|הַקַּדְמֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּם֙\rb*,\f + \fr 2:20 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f*
\q2 \rb and its rear guard|וְסֹפ֖וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Western|הָאַֽחֲר֑וֹן\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֣ם\rb*.\f + \fr 2:20 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea\f*
\q1 \rb And its stench|בָאְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb will rise|וְעָלָ֣ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb its foul odor|צַחֲנָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb will ascend|וְתַ֙עַל֙\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He has done|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb great things|הִגְדִּ֖יל\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְאִ֖י\rb*, \rb O land|אֲדָמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb rejoice|גִּ֣ילִי\rb* \rb and be glad|וּשְׂמָ֔חִי\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has done|לַעֲשֽׂוֹת׃\rb* \rb great things|הִגְדִּ֥יל\rb*.
\q1 \v 22 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְאוּ֙\rb*, \rb O beasts|בַּהֲמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the field|שָׂדַ֔י\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the open|מִדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb pastures|נְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb have turned green|דָשְׁא֖וּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb the trees|עֵץ֙\rb* \rb bear|נָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb their fruit|פִרְי֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the fig tree|תְּאֵנָ֥ה\rb* \rb and vine|וָגֶ֖פֶן\rb* \rb yield|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb their best|חֵילָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:22 \ft Literally \fqa their strength\f*
\q1 \v 23 \rb Be glad|גִּ֤ילוּ\rb*, \rb O children|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zion|צִיּ֗וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and rejoice|וְשִׂמְחוּ֙\rb* \rb in the LORD|בַּיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He has given|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the autumn rains|הַמּוֹרֶ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb for your vindication|לִצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb He sends|וַיּ֣וֹרֶד\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb showers|גֶּ֛שֶׁם\rb*,
\q2 \rb both autumn|מוֹרֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and spring rains|וּמַלְק֖וֹשׁ\rb*, \rb as before|בָּרִאשֽׁוֹן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 24 \rb The threshing floors|הַגֳּרָנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb will be full of|וּמָלְא֥וּ\rb* \rb grain|בָּ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the vats|הַיְקָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb will overflow|וְהֵשִׁ֥יקוּ\rb* \rb with new wine|תִּיר֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb and oil|וְיִצְהָֽר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 25 \rb I will repay|וְשִׁלַּמְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the years|הַשָּׁנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb eaten by locusts|אָכַ֣ל\rb* —
\q2 \rb the swarming locust|הָֽאַרְבֶּ֔ה\rb*, \rb the young locust|הַיֶּ֖לֶק\rb*,
\q1 \rb the destroying locust|וְהֶחָסִ֣יל\rb*, \rb and the devouring locust|וְהַגָּזָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:25 \ft The precise identification of the four kinds of insects mentioned here is uncertain.\f*—
\q2 \rb My great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb army|חֵילִי֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I sent|שִׁלַּ֖חְתִּי\rb* \rb against you|בָּכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 26 \rb You will have plenty to eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אָכוֹל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb until you are satisfied|וְשָׂב֔וֹעַ\rb*.
\q1 \rb You will praise|וְהִלַּלְתֶּ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has worked|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb wonders|לְהַפְלִ֑יא\rb* \rb for you|עִמָּכֶ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb will never again|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*
\q2 \rb be put to shame|יֵבֹ֥שׁוּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb am present in|בְקֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and that I|וַאֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and there is no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb other|ע֑וֹד\rb*.
\q1 \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb will never again|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb be put to shame|יֵבֹ֥שׁוּ\rb*.
\s1 I Will Pour Out My Spirit
\r (\ref Acts 2:14–36|ACT 2:14-36\ref*)
\q1 \v 28 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb afterward|אַֽחֲרֵי־\rb*,\rb |כֵ֗ן\rb* \rb I will pour out|אֶשְׁפּ֤וֹךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Spirit|רוּחִי֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb people|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*.
\q2 \rb Your sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will prophesy|וְנִבְּא֖וּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb your old|זִקְנֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb men will dream dreams|יַחֲלֹמ֔וּן\rb*\rb |חֲלֹמ֣וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb your young men|בַּח֣וּרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will see|יִרְאֽוּ׃\rb* \rb visions|חֶזְיֹנ֖וֹת\rb*.
\q1 \v 29 \rb Even|וְגַ֥ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb My menservants|הָֽעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb maidservants|הַשְּׁפָח֑וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will pour out|אֶשְׁפּ֖וֹךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Spirit|רוּחִֽי׃\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֔מָּה\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 30 \rb I will show|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb* \rb wonders|מֽוֹפְתִ֔ים\rb* \rb in the heavens|בַּשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and on the earth|וּבָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb blood|דָּ֣ם\rb* \rb and fire|וָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and columns|וְתִֽימֲר֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 2:30 \ft LXX \fqa clouds \ft or \fqa billows\f* \rb of smoke|עָשָֽׁן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 31 \rb The sun|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb will be turned|יֵהָפֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb to darkness|לְחֹ֔שֶׁךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the moon|וְהַיָּרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb to blood|לְדָ֑ם\rb*
\q2 \rb before|לִפְנֵ֗י\rb* \rb the coming|בּ֚וֹא\rb* \rb of the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb and awesome|וְהַנּוֹרָֽא׃\rb*\f + \fr 2:31 \ft Or \fqa dreadful\ft ; LXX \fqa glorious\f* \rb Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb And|וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb everyone|כֹּ֧ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb calls|יִקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be saved|יִמָּלֵ֑ט\rb*;\f + \fr 2:32 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 2:17–21|ACT 2:17-21\ref* and Romans 10:13\f*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb on Mount|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb Zion|צִיּ֨וֹן\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb*
\q2 \rb there will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb deliverance|פְלֵיטָ֗ה\rb*, \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has promised|אָמַ֣ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb among the remnant|וּבַ֨שְּׂרִידִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb called|קֹרֵֽא׃\rb* \rb by the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.[’’]
\c 3
\s1 The LORD Judges the Nations
\q1 \v 1 “\rb Yes|כִּ֗י\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb and at that|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֣ת\rb*,
\q2 \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I restore|אָשׁוּב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁב֥וּת\rb*,\f + \fr 3:1 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Judah and Jerusalem\f*
\q1 \v 2 \rb I will gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and bring them down|וְה֣וֹרַדְתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb*.\f + \fr 3:2 \fqa Jehoshaphat \ft means \fqa the LORD judges\ft ; also in verse 12.\f*
\q1 \rb There|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb I will enter into judgment|וְנִשְׁפַּטְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb against them|עִמָּ֜ם\rb*
\q2 \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֨י\rb*, \rb My inheritance|וְנַחֲלָתִ֤י\rb*, \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have scattered|פִּזְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb among the nations|בַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they divided up|חִלֵּֽקוּ׃\rb* \rb My land|אַרְצִ֖י\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb They cast|יַדּ֣וּ\rb* \rb lots|גוֹרָ֑ל\rb* \rb for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֖י\rb*;
\q2 \rb they bartered|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb a boy|הַיֶּ֙לֶד֙\rb* \rb for a prostitute|בַּזּוֹנָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and sold|מָכְר֥וּ\rb* \rb a girl|וְהַיַּלְדָּ֛ה\rb* \rb for wine|בַיַּ֖יִן\rb* \rb to drink|וַיִּשְׁתּֽוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Now|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb do you have|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb against Me|לִי֙\rb*, \rb O Tyre|צֹ֣ר\rb*, \rb Sidon|וְצִיד֔וֹן\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the regions|גְּלִיל֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Philistia|פְּלָ֑שֶׁת\rb*? \rb Are you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb rendering|מְשַׁלְּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb against Me|עָלָ֔י\rb* \rb a recompense|הַגְּמ֗וּל\rb*? \rb If|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb retaliate|גֹּמְלִ֤ים\rb* \rb against Me|עָלַ֔י\rb*, \rb I will swiftly|קַ֣ל\rb* \rb and speedily|מְהֵרָ֔ה\rb* \rb return|אָשִׁ֥יב\rb* \rb your recompense|גְּמֻלְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb upon your heads|בְּרֹאשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb For|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you took|לְקַחְתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb My silver|כַּסְפִּ֥י\rb* \rb and gold|וּזְהָבִ֖י\rb* \rb and carried off|הֲבֵאתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb My finest|הַטֹּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb treasures|וּמַֽחֲמַדַּי֙\rb* \rb to your temples|לְהֵיכְלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 3:5 \ft Or \fqa palaces\f* \v 6 \rb You sold|מְכַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the people|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb to the Greeks|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַיְּוָנִ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Or \fqa to the peoples of Javan\f* \rb to|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb send them far|הַרְחִיקָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb their homeland|גְּבוּלָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֣י\rb*, \rb I will rouse them|מְעִירָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the places|הַ֨מָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you sold|מְכַרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb*; \rb I will return|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb your recompense|גְמֻלְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb upon your heads|בְּרֹאשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I will sell|וּמָכַרְתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and daughters|בְּנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of the people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and they will sell them|וּמְכָר֥וּם\rb* \rb to the Sabeans|לִשְׁבָאיִ֖ם\rb* — \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a distant|רָח֑וֹק\rb* \rb nation|גּ֣וֹי\rb*.”
\p \rb Indeed|כִּ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Proclaim|קִרְאוּ־\rb* \rb this|זֹאת֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*:
\b 
\q1 “\rb Prepare|קַדְּשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb for war|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb rouse|הָעִ֙ירוּ֙\rb* \rb the mighty men|הַגִּבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb*;
\q1 \rb let all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*
\q2 \rb advance|יִגְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb and attack|יַֽעֲל֔וּ\rb*!
\q1 \v 10 \rb Beat|כֹּ֤תּוּ\rb* \rb your plowshares|אִתֵּיכֶם֙\rb* \rb into swords|לַֽחֲרָב֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and your pruning hooks|וּמַזְמְרֹֽתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into spears|לִרְמָחִ֑ים\rb*.
\q2 \rb Let the weak|הַֽחַלָּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb say|יֹאמַ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb I am|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb strong|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb*!’
\q1 \v 11 \rb Come|וָבֹ֧אוּ\rb* \rb quickly|ע֣וּשׁוּ\rb*, \rb all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb you surrounding|מִסָּבִ֖יב\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and gather yourselves|וְנִקְבָּ֑צוּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Bring down|הַֽנְחַ֥ת\rb* \rb Your mighty ones|גִּבּוֹרֶֽיךָ׃\rb*\rb |שָׁ֕מָּה\rb*,
\q2 \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Let the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb be roused|יֵע֙וֹרוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and advance|וְיַעֲל֣וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Valley|עֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהֽוֹשָׁפָ֑ט\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb I will sit down|אֵשֵׁ֛ב\rb*
\q2 \rb to judge|לִשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Swing|שִׁלְח֣וּ\rb* \rb the sickle|מַגָּ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the harvest|קָצִ֑יר\rb* \rb is ripe|בָשַׁ֖ל\rb*.\f + \fr 3:13 \ft LXX \fqa the harvest has come\ft ; see also \ref Mark 4:29|MRK 4:29\ref*.\f*
\q1 \rb Come|בֹּ֤אֽוּ\rb*, \rb trample the grapes|רְדוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the winepress|גַּ֔ת\rb* \rb is full|מָ֣לְאָה\rb*;
\q1 \rb the wine vats|הַיְקָבִ֔ים\rb* \rb overflow|הֵשִׁ֙יקוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb their wickedness|רָעָתָֽם׃\rb* \rb is great|רַבָּ֖ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb Multitudes|הֲמוֹנִ֣ים\rb*, \rb multitudes|הֲמוֹנִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in the valley|בְּעֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of decision|הֶֽחָר֑וּץ\rb*!
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is near|קָרוֹב֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in the valley|בְּעֵ֖מֶק\rb* \rb of decision|הֶחָרֽוּץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb The sun|שֶׁ֥מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and moon|וְיָרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb will grow dark|קָדָ֑רוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the stars|וְכוֹכָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb will no longer|אָסְפ֥וּ\rb* \rb shine|נָגְהָֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb The LORD|וַיהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb will roar|יִשְׁאָ֗ג\rb* \rb from Zion|מִצִּיּ֣וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and raise|יִתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb His voice|קוֹל֔וֹ\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|וּמִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb heaven|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb and earth|וָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb will tremble|וְרָעֲשׁ֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb But the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb will be a refuge|מַֽחֲסֶ֣ה\rb* \rb for His people|לְעַמּ֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb a stronghold|וּמָע֖וֹז\rb* \rb for the people|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\s1 Blessings for God’s People
\q1 \v 17 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb who dwells|שֹׁכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in Zion|בְּצִיּ֣וֹן\rb*, \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb mountain|הַר־\rb*.
\q1 \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb holy|קֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*,
\q2 \rb never|לֹא־\rb* \rb again|עֽוֹד׃ס\rb* \rb to be overrun|יַֽעַבְרוּ־\rb* \rb by foreigners|וְזָרִ֥ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb And|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb in that|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶהָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb will drip|יִטְּפ֧וּ\rb* \rb with sweet wine|עָסִ֗יס\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the hills|וְהַגְּבָעוֹת֙\rb* \rb will flow|תֵּלַ֣כְנָה\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָ֔ב\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the streams|אֲפִיקֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb will run|יֵ֣לְכוּ\rb* \rb with water|מָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and a spring|וּמַעְיָ֗ן\rb* \rb will flow|יֵצֵ֔א\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb to water|וְהִשְׁקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Valley|נַ֥חַל\rb* \rb of Acacias|הַשִּׁטִּֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 3:18 \ft Or \fqa Valley of Shittim\f*
\q1 \v 19 \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb will become|תִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb desolate|לִשְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Edom|וֶאֱד֕וֹם\rb* \rb a desert|לְמִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb wasteland|שְׁמָמָ֖ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb because of the violence|מֵֽחֲמַס֙\rb* \rb done to the people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb land|בְּאַרְצָֽם׃\rb* \rb they shed|שָׁפְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֖יא\rb* \rb blood|דָם־\rb*.
\q1 \v 20 \rb But Judah|וִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb will be inhabited forever|תֵּשֵׁ֑ב\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and Jerusalem|וִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb from generation|לְד֥וֹר\rb* \rb to generation|וָדֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 21 \rb For I will avenge|וְנִקֵּ֖יתִי\rb* \rb their blood|דָּמָ֣ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb which I have not yet|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb avenged|נִקֵּ֑יתִי\rb*.\f + \fr 3:21 \ft Or \fqa For I will pardon their bloodguilt, which I have not yet pardoned.\f*”
\qr \rb For the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb dwells|שֹׁכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb in Zion|בְּצִיּֽוֹן׃\rb*.
